# Local-only agent guidance (not published; comments in tracked files must not
# reference these)
CLAUDE.md
RULES.md
task.md
PLAN.md
.claude/

# A local set of captures for the offline proofs to run against. These are NOT
# this project's to publish: a capture is a recording made by whoever trained
# it, under their own terms, and the code's MIT grant does not reach it. The
# plug-in ships none and resolves no bank by a tracked path — the four banks are
# whatever the user loaded — so nothing here depends on this directory existing.
# The proofs find it through --captures or $RATIONS_TEST_CAPTURES.
#
# Keep it that way: a capture committed here is a capture republished to
# everyone who clones, and deleting it later does not take it back out of the
# history.
captures/

# Personal CMake configure presets (local reference-tree paths).
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Build directories
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# CMake generated
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile
*.cmake
!CMakeLists.txt
# ...but cmake/ holds SOURCE scripts, not generated ones — the MinGW toolchain
# file lives there and is named on the configure command line, so without this
# negation the blanket *.cmake above would keep it out of a fresh clone and the
# Windows build would be unreproducible. Generated .cmake files all live under
# the build directories already ignored above.
!cmake/*.cmake

# Compiled output
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.vst3

# Release archives produced by scripts/makedist-linux.sh — these are attached
# to GitHub releases, not committed.
dist/
*.tar.gz
*.tar.xz
*.zip

